"reflections/index.md","dataUrl":"/index-4.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"sJSA9gdwhM"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"\n---\n\n## My Learning Journey\n\nThroughout this course, I explored how Deep Learning can\nbe used to solve problems involving data, images, and\nother complex patterns.\n\nMy work focuses not only on building models, but also on\nunderstanding:\n\n- How neural networks learn\n- How data is prepared for deep learning\n- How models are trained and optimized\n- How model performance is evaluated\n- How different architectures affect results\n- How experiments can be interpreted and improved\n\n---\n\n## Tools & Technologies\n\nSome of the tools and technologies used throughout my\nlearning journey include:\n\n`Python` · `Jupyter Notebook` · `NumPy` · `Pandas` ·\n`Matplotlib` · `Scikit-learn` · `PyTorch` · `TensorFlow`\n\n---\n\n## Portfolio Structure\n\n```{list-table}\n:header-rows: 0\n:widths: 25 75\n\n* - 🧠 Learning Journey\n  - Concepts, techniques, and knowledge developed throughout the course.\n\n* - 🧪 Labs\n  - Hands-on laboratory activities and experiments.\n\n* - 📝 Assignments\n  - Individual course requirements and exercises.\n\n* - 🚀 Projects\n  - Larger applications of Deep Learning concepts.\n\n* - 💭 Reflections\n  - Personal evaluation of my progress and learning experience.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"j4EJNBKRKs"}],"key":"Akq380KQAv"}],"key":"h3ayKbYsFn"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}}}